#!ipxe
# Boot this machine from its own network disk on the pxe stack's iscsi
# service. The disk is found by the machine's MAC address, so this file is the
# same for every machine; only its name differs.
#
# Where it goes: the TFTP root on the boot host, as the host script of each
# machine (MAC lower-case, with hyphens), e.g.
#   dockerdata/pxe/tftp/ipxe/hosts/52-54-00-09-01-02.ipxe
# boot.ipxe runs it before Matchbox and the menu. (A Matchbox profile has only
# a kernel, initrds and arguments: it cannot say sanboot.)
#
# The disk: dockerdata/pxe/iscsi/disks/debian-<mac>.raw, e.g. made with
#   docker exec pxe-iscsi-1 iscsi-disk copy debian debian-52-54-00-09-01-02
# For another base or name scheme, change the target name below.
#
# Root path: iscsi:<server>:<protocol>:<port>:<LUN>:<target>. LUN 1: tgt's
# LUN 0 is its controller, and iPXE's default LUN 0 fails with an
# input/output error. ${next-server} is the boot server (dnsmasq's address);
# write the address instead if your DHCP setup gives another one.
# The OS on the disk must bring its own iSCSI client that takes over from the
# firmware table iPXE leaves (iBFT); get-debian-iscsi-disk.sh prepares Debian
# so.

echo Booting from iSCSI disk debian-${netX/mac:hexhyp} on ${next-server}
sanboot iscsi:${next-server}:::1:iqn.2026-11.pxe.stack:debian-${netX/mac:hexhyp} || goto failed

:failed
echo sanboot failed: is there a disk debian-${netX/mac:hexhyp} (iscsi-disk list)?
echo Going on with the normal boot in 5 seconds
sleep 5
exit 1
